BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Ishizue Award Dinner 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T210000
UID:347d8d1f18cfb5c9917f91900a7007a9@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:The JCCC Board of Directors is pleased to announce that the 8t
 h Ishizue Award and accompanying dinner will be held on Thursday November 
 19\, 2026. The Ishizue Award acknowledges and expresses our appreciation a
 nd respect to members or friends who have made exceptional contributions t
 o the Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre. The name Ishizue\, meaning corner
 stone or foundation\, pays tribute to the 75 families who\, at significant
  personal financial risk\, guaranteed the original mortgage on the JCCC at
  123 Wynford Drive in the early 1960’s. These families provided the foun
 dation upon which the JCCC was built\, and their support for the JCCC will
  forever be recognized as the cornerstone for who we are as a community. T
 he recipients of this annual award are a very distinguished group of peopl
 e who have each made significant life contributions to the Japanese Canadi
 an Cultural Centre. They are: Ken Fukushima Harry Kawabe Akiko Maruoka Dav
 id Ohashi (Post humous) Connie Sugiyama David Tsubouchi We cordially invit
 e you to honour these distinguished award recipients at an intimate and el
 egant dinner on Thursday November 19th at 6:30pm at the Japanese Canadian 
 Cultural Centre. Black tie optional. Tickets are $180 each (plus HST) . Ma
 ximum of 10 guests per table. To purchase tickets please order through the
  button below or in person at the JCCC\, starting September 21\, 2026\, an
 d ending November 9\, 2026. Please contact Sharon Marubashi for any furthe
 r information by email or phone (647-291-4751). On behalf of all of the di
 rectors of the Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre\, we look forward to spen
 ding a special evening of recognition and celebration together. Purchase T
 icket Agenda Cocktails Dinner Evening's Greetings Catering by Spectrum Cat
 ering Entertainment Koto Performance by Aiko Fujii Greetings from JCCC Pre
 sident Chris Hope Award Ceremony Group Photo Closing Remarks Aiko Fujii Ai
 ko Fujii started learning at the Ikuta School of Koto and Jiuta Shamisen a
 t an early age. She is a licensed teacher at Kyoto Todokai School of Koto 
 and Shamisen. In addition to performing\, she is actively involved in cros
 s-genre collaborations and teaching.\n\nCategories: Community Event\, Soci
 al
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/ishizue-award-dinner-2026
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
